{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.SchurWeyl.TwoRowIdxReindex","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.TwoRowIdxReindex","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.SchurWeyl.WtraceRadicalSemisimple","lean:module:QOU.SchurWeyl.MarkovConventionD"],"declarations":14,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.TwoRowIdxReindex.range_sum_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.TwoRowIdxReindex.range_sum_pos","kind":"theorem","line":176,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/TwoRowIdxReindex.lean#L176-L183","doc":"**The reindexed sum is strictly positive**, so the identity above is not `0 = 0`.\nInherited from `finrank_traceQuot_pos`, which in turn reuses `traceQuot_one_ne_zero`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.TwoRowIdxReindex.finrank_traceQuot_eq_range_sum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.TwoRowIdxReindex.finrank_traceQuot_eq_range_sum","kind":"theorem","line":140,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/TwoRowIdxReindex.lean#L140-L173","doc":"**`finrank_traceQuot`, reindexed by second-row length.**\n\n    finrank R (H_n(q)/rad(wtrace)) = Σ_{k ≤ ⌊(n+1)/2⌋} (#SYT (n+1−k, k))²\n\nthe shape `QOU.Mathlib.TwoRowDimCatalan.dimHLF_two_row_sq_sum` sums in, so the two are now\ndirectly comparable.\n\n🛑 **This is still a tableau COUNT, not `dimHLF`.**  Comparing it to `catalan (n+1)` needs the\nhook length formula at general `n`, which is absent from Mathlib and proved in this corpus only\nfor `n ≤ 4` plus `n = 5`.  That is the single remaining gap, and it is the whole point of this\nfile that it is now single. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.TwoRowIdxReindex.twoRowDim_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.TwoRowIdxReindex.twoRowDim_eq","kind":"theorem","line":134,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/TwoRowIdxReindex.lean#L134-L136","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.TwoRowIdxReindex.twoRowDim","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.TwoRowIdxReindex.twoRowDim","kind":"def","line":129,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/TwoRowIdxReindex.lean#L129-L132","doc":"The standard-tableau count of `twoRow m k`, extended by `0` off `k ≤ m` so that it is a\ntotal function of `(m, k)` and can be summed over a bare `Finset.range`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.TwoRowIdxReindex.twoRowIdxEquiv_apply","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.TwoRowIdxReindex.twoRowIdxEquiv_apply","kind":"theorem","line":124,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/TwoRowIdxReindex.lean#L124-L125","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.TwoRowIdxReindex.twoRowIdxEquiv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.TwoRowIdxReindex.twoRowIdxEquiv","kind":"def","line":113,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/TwoRowIdxReindex.lean#L113-L122","doc":"**`TwoRowIdx n ≃ Fin ((n+1)/2 + 1)`**, by second-row length.\n\nForward is \"read off the second row\"; backward is `ofSecondRow`.  The two round trips are\n`secondRow_ofSecondRow` and `ofSecondRow_secondRow`, the second of which is where\n`partitionShape_injective` is spent. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.TwoRowIdxReindex.ofSecondRow_secondRow","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.TwoRowIdxReindex.ofSecondRow_secondRow","kind":"theorem","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/TwoRowIdxReindex.lean#L100-L109","doc":"The round trip the other way: a partition is recovered from its second-row length.  This is\nwhere `partitionShape_injective` is spent, and it is why the `choose` above is harmless. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.TwoRowIdxReindex.secondRow_ofSecondRow","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.TwoRowIdxReindex.secondRow_ofSecondRow","kind":"theorem","line":96,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/TwoRowIdxReindex.lean#L96-L98","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.TwoRowIdxReindex.shape_ofSecondRow","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.TwoRowIdxReindex.shape_ofSecondRow","kind":"theorem","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/TwoRowIdxReindex.lean#L91-L94","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.TwoRowIdxReindex.ofSecondRow","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.TwoRowIdxReindex.ofSecondRow","kind":"def","line":80,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/TwoRowIdxReindex.lean#L80-L89","doc":"**The at-most-two-row partition of `n + 1` with second row `k`.**  Obtained from\n`exists_partitionShape_eq` on `twoRow (n + 1 - k) k`; the choice is harmless because\n`partitionShape` is injective, which is what `ofSecondRow_secondRow` below spends. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.TwoRowIdxReindex.secondRow_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.TwoRowIdxReindex.secondRow_le","kind":"theorem","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/TwoRowIdxReindex.lean#L69-L76","doc":"The second row is at most half of `n + 1` — it is the shorter of two rows summing to\n`n + 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.TwoRowIdxReindex.rowLen_add","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.TwoRowIdxReindex.rowLen_add","kind":"theorem","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/TwoRowIdxReindex.lean#L61-L67","doc":"The two row lengths sum to `n + 1`.  `eq_twoRow_of_rowLen_two_eq_zero` turns the shape into\na `twoRow`, and `card_twoRow` then reads the cell count off it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.TwoRowIdxReindex.twoRow_congr","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.TwoRowIdxReindex.twoRow_congr","kind":"theorem","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/TwoRowIdxReindex.lean#L52-L57","doc":"**`twoRow` depends only on its two row lengths.**  The `k ≤ m` argument is a `Prop`, so\nproof irrelevance closes it after `subst`; needed because `rw` cannot rewrite inside that\nargument (the motive stops being type correct). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.TwoRowIdxReindex.rowLen_twoRow_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.TwoRowIdxReindex.rowLen_twoRow_two","kind":"theorem","line":43,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/TwoRowIdxReindex.lean#L43-L50","doc":"**`twoRow` has no third row.**  Not in `OcneanuWeightBranching`, which stops at\n`rowLen_twoRow_one`; three lines off `mem_twoRow`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}